  "title": "RTP: Have shim header dissector return 0 on error",
  "description": "The RTP shim header dissector returns the number of bytes consumed\nto dissect the RTP header. However when an unknown version number\nis encountered the current offset is returned. That should be the\nnumber of bytes consumed, i.e. 0.\nFix the user of this function to handle this situation properly.",
